cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Extraction of Robust Commands from SSVEP Signals for Use in Brain–Computer Interfaces"
authors:
  - family-names: "Danesh Amooz"
    given-names: "Farooq"
    affiliation: "University of Tabriz, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering"
date-released: 2026-08-12
url: "https://github.com/<your-username>/ssvep-robust-bci"
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-username>/ssvep-robust-bci"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >
  A five-key SSVEP/c-VEP brain-computer interface control panel for wheelchair
  control, with a literature review organizing SSVEP-BCI decoding methods by
  a three-dimensional robustness taxonomy (within-trial noise, cross-subject/
  low-calibration, and adversarial robustness), and three proposed, testable
  robustness mechanisms (H1: color+frequency redundancy; H2: trial-by-trial
  online adaptation; H3: code-modulated STOP key).
keywords:
  - brain-computer-interface
  - SSVEP
  - cVEP
  - EEG
  - assistive-technology
  - wheelchair-control
